       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-26 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Anthropic Leverages Cross-Selling to Retain Enterprise Clients</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Anthropic’s recent IPO filing reveals a successful cross-selling strategy, with over half of customers spending $100,000-plus annually now utilizing both the Claude platform and first-party applications. This integrated ecosystem, similar to models used by Amazon and Uber, has driven net revenue retention to approximately 900% as of the third quarter.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/anthropic-leverages-cross-selling-to-retain-enterprise-clien.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Anthropic attributes this growth to customers expanding Claude’s deployment across their organizations. The company reports that its highest-spending enterprise users who utilize tools like Claude Code spend roughly 20 times more per month than average users, validating the effectiveness of embedding applications directly into existing enterprise technology stacks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects the IPO filing details and the cross-selling strategy described in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/26/anthropics-ipo-filing-reveals-its-strategy-for-keeping-enterprise-customers-hooked/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
