     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-26 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>BCCI Sets November 15 Deadline for IPL 2027 Player Retentions</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#IPL</span> <span>#BCCI</span> <span>#Player Auction</span></div>
       <p>The Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) has set November 15, 2026, as the deadline for all ten Indian Premier League (IPL) franchises to submit their retention lists. This crucial date comes approximately one month before the IPL 2027 player mini-auction, which is scheduled for December 16, 2026, in Goa. IPL executives communicated this cut-off to franchises through official channels.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/bcci-sets-november-15-deadline-for-ipl-2027-player-retention.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>BCCI secretary Devajit Saikia had previously confirmed the auction date and venue in October. This December auction marks the final mini-auction within the IPL's current 2023-27 cycle, with a mega-auction confirmed to precede the 2028 season. The decisions made regarding retentions and trades in the coming weeks are therefore highly consequential for long-term squad planning.</p><p>Goa will host the auction, marking its return to Indian soil after three consecutive overseas editions held in Saudi Arabia, Dubai, and Abu Dhabi. Notably, the December 16 auction date coincides with the second One Day International between India and Sri Lanka, scheduled for Bengaluru.</p><p>The trade window, which opened one month after the IPL 2026 final, has already seen two significant deals. Under IPL rules, the window remains open until one week before the auction, setting the trade deadline at December 9, 2026. It will then reopen one month prior to the 2027 season. Among the reported trades, Lucknow Super Giants released captain Rishabh Pant to Delhi Capitals in exchange for left-arm wrist-spinner Kuldeep Yadav. Subsequently, the Capitals traded pacer T. Natarajan to Sunrisers Hyderabad for uncapped leg-spinner Zeeshan Ansari. Franchises are now evaluating their squads and remaining salary purses to strategise for further trades or a larger auction budget. While the BCCI had earmarked a March 14 to May 30 window for the 2027 edition, Saikia indicated in September that the tournament could start towards the end of March, though official confirmation is pending.</p><p>What to watch: Franchises will finalize retention lists and trade decisions by November 15.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is comprehensive, well-structured, and correctly incorporates all relevant details regarding the IPL retention deadline, auction logistics, and trade window mechanics provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/bcci-sets-november-15-as-ipl-2027-retention-deadline-ahead-of-auction-3582/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
