       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-10-26 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Chris Hemsworth and Elsa Pataky Transform Byron Bay Estate Into Modern Mansion</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Hollywood actor Chris Hemsworth and his wife, Elsa Pataky, purchased a 4.2-hectare coastal property near Byron Bay, Australia, for A$7 million in 2014. They demolished the existing eight-bedroom Balinese-style residence and replaced it with a modern mansion featuring six bedrooms, a gym, and a 50-metre rooftop infinity pool. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/chris-hemsworth-and-elsa-pataky-transform-byron-bay-estate-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The estate, located at Broken Head, underwent extensive redevelopment with construction costs estimated at approximately A$8.8 million in 2019. Recent reports highlighted further additions to the property, including a tennis court, a dirt-bike track, and a skateboard ramp alongside hundreds of installed solar panels.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Strong density, covers purchase, transformation, and recent updates accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
