     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-26 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Court to Hear Actor Imran Khan's Plea Against Leave India Notice</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actor Imran Khan’s petition challenging the Centre’s Leave India Notice will be heard on Tuesday, just one day prior to the October 28 deadline. The hearing was postponed on Monday after the Centre, Khan's legal representation, and an intervening petitioner all requested additional time for arguments. Khan, holding Overseas Citizen of India status, received the notice from the Foreigners Regional Registration Office following his alleged participation in a protest against the Chief Election Commissioner.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/court-to-hear-actor-imran-khans-plea-against-leave-india-not.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In his plea, Khan denied ties to the protest organizers, claiming he visited August Kranti Maidan merely out of curiosity. He stated he complied with police orders to leave but was subsequently detained while speaking with media personnel. Meanwhile, an intervening party filed a plea supporting the government action, alleging Khan showed a lack of seriousness regarding the law.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and concise. It omits the specific name of the political party mentioned in the intervention but covers all essential legal and situational facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/actor-imran-khan-plea-against-leave-india-notice-heard-a-day-before-october-28-deadline-cjp-protest-3025486-2026-10-26?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-26/court-to-hear-actor-imran-khans-plea-against-leave-india-not" data-title="Court to Hear Actor Imran Khan's Plea Against Leave India Notice"><b>Share:</b>
