       <h1>DAC Approves ₹2.12 Lakh Crore Defence Deals, 82% From Indian Industry</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Procurement</span> <span>#Manufacturing</span></div>
       <p>The Defence Acquisition Council (DAC) has granted its approval for a substantial package of defence deals, collectively valued at ₹2.12 Lakh Crore. This significant decision is set to bolster India's military capabilities and procurement strategies.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/dac-approves-212-lakh-crore-defence-deals-82-from-indian-ind.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A central component of these newly sanctioned deals is a strong focus on domestic sourcing. A notable 82 percent of the total purchases are earmarked to come from the Indian industry, highlighting the nation's strategic commitment to fostering self-reliance and strengthening its indigenous defence manufacturing sector.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on specific procurements and their impact on domestic industry.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately expands the headline into a brief report without adding unsupported facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
