       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-26 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Deep Depression in Bay of Bengal Forecast to Become Severe Cyclone</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A deep depression in the Bay of Bengal is intensifying and is projected to strike the Andhra Pradesh coast between Bapatla and Visakhapatnam on October 28. According to the India Meteorological Department, the system is expected to escalate into a very severe cyclonic storm.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/deep-depression-in-bay-of-bengal-forecast-to-become-severe-c.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Authorities have issued warnings for extremely heavy rainfall and strong winds across coastal Andhra Pradesh and Odisha beginning October 27. The weather system, currently located approximately 820 km east-southeast of Visakhapatnam, poses a significant threat to standing paddy and coastal crops as it continues its westward movement.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the meteorological forecast and location details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
