       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-26 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Early Users Report Screen Cracking Issues on Apple's New iPhone Duo</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Apple's newly launched foldable phone, the iPhone Duo, is facing early user complaints regarding screens cracking after hours or days of use. Bloomberg reported that early adopters experienced display malfunctions and loud crunching noises preceding cracks, while 404 Media noted significant creases down the middle of the $2,000 folding screens.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/early-users-report-screen-cracking-issues-on-apples-new-ipho.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Apple told Bloomberg that it is aware of an issue impacting the inner display on a small number of iPhone Duo units. The device was announced at the Surprise and Shine event following long-standing industry ambitions to create a functional foldable phone.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures the core reporting cleanly and within tight length constraints.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/26/uh-oh-it-sounds-like-the-iphone-duo-keeps-cracking-and-users-arent-happy-about-it/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
