     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-26 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Infosys Shares Decline Following Q2 Miss and Guidance Cut</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Infosys</span> <span>#Stock Market</span> <span>#IT Sector</span> <span>#Earnings</span></div>
       <p>Infosys shares dropped over 3.5 per cent on Monday, trading as low as ₹1,109.70 on the BSE, following the company's second-quarter earnings report. Bengaluru-based Infosys posted a 6.2 per cent rise in net profit to ₹7,828 crore and a 10.7 per cent revenue increase to ₹49,244 crore. However, these figures missed analyst expectations, which had predicted a net profit of ₹7,904 crore and revenue of ₹49,108 crore. The company subsequently reduced its FY27 revenue growth guidance to 1-2 per cent year-on-year, down from the previous range of 1.5-3.0 per cent.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/infosys-shares-decline-following-q2-miss-and-guidance-cut.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>So far this year, Infosys shares have remained 31 per cent lower, reflecting a broader selloff in traditional IT services driven by fears of AI-led deflation. Analysts at Motilal Oswal Financial Services (MOFSL) noted that competitive intensity and wage hikes are weighing on margins. While maintaining a 'BUY' rating with a target price of ₹1,300, MOFSL trimmed its EPS estimates by up to 2 per cent. Emkay Global also reduced its EPS estimates, citing the Q2 miss and guidance cut, while retaining a target price of ₹1,300.</p><p>Conversely, Antique Stock Broking highlighted a silver lining in the form of $5.2 billion in large-deal total contract value (TCV), which surpassed its estimate of $4 billion. This included a seven-year mega deal worth over $2 billion with a financial services client. Despite this, they maintained a 'HOLD' rating with a target price of ₹1,115, citing the guidance cut as a near-term headwind.</p><p>What to watch: Future deal conversion rates and the impact of AI-led productivity deflation on long-term margins.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report accurately summarizes the financial performance, analyst outlook, and market context provided in the text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/infosys-shares-drop-4-on-q2-guidance-miss-check-what-analysts-recommend-126102600141_1.html" rel="noopener">BS Personal Finance</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
