       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-26 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Mumbai Court Extends Custody in Tiger Shroff Attack Case</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Mumbai court extended the police custody of four suspects—Kunal, Sumit, Radha, and Babita—until October 28 in connection with the October 18 shooting at actor Tiger Shroff's car. Investigators require the extension to collect voice samples and verify data recovered from the accused's phones.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/mumbai-court-extends-custody-in-tiger-shroff-attack-case.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Police allege the group used the Signal app to coordinate, with Radha delivering weapons provided by Kunal. The suspects reportedly used fake identities to book hotels. Authorities have already recovered two pistols and ten cartridges, while an additional suspect remains detained in Indore.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the police investigation details and the court proceedings while adhering to the word count.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/mumbai/tiger-shroff-attack-police-custody-of-4-extended-till-october-28-voice-samples-needed-say-cops/article71627255.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
