       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-26 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Paytm Reports 10-Fold Net Profit Jump to ₹225 Crore in Q2FY27</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Business</span> <span>#Earnings</span> <span>#Paytm</span> <span>#AI</span></div>
       <p>Paytm has reported a significant financial performance for the second quarter of fiscal year 2027 (Q2FY27). The company's net profit soared 10-fold, reaching ₹225 crore, indicating a period of robust growth for the digital payments firm.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/paytm-reports-10-fold-net-profit-jump-to-225-crore-in-q2fy27.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the same quarter, Paytm's operating revenue also saw a healthy increase, rising by 28 percent year-over-year (YoY) to ₹2,648 crore. This revenue growth was primarily driven by sustained momentum across its merchant and consumer businesses, alongside expanded monetisation efforts and the strategic adoption of artificial intelligence (AI).</p><p>What to watch: Continued impact of AI adoption on future financial performance.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, concise, and faithfully reflects all provided financial data.</p>
