       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-26 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Political Line Newsletter Examines Federalism and State-Level Tensions</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The latest edition of the Political Line newsletter, curated by Varghese K. George, addresses rising federalist tensions in India. The piece highlights Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s critique of federalism discussions as separatist, alongside remarks from Uttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath comparing other states to Kashmir, Kerala, and West Bengal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/political-line-newsletter-examines-federalism-and-state-leve.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The newsletter also analyzes the Haryana government’s attempt to restore a state law reserving 75% of private jobs for locals, which challenges national constitutional norms. Additionally, it notes Tamil Nadu's ongoing efforts to reclaim medical school admission powers through the NEET Exemption Bill, despite resistance from the state Governor.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the newsletter's themes, though it attributes a February 2022 newsletter date to a 2026 article.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
