     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-26 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Rural India: Girls' Secondary Education Completion Lags Boys</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Rural India</span> <span>#Gender Disparity</span> <span>#UNESCO</span></div>
       <p>A report by UNESCO highlights a significant disparity in upper secondary education completion rates in rural India. According to the findings, only 59 girls complete upper secondary education for every 100 boys in rural areas.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-26/rural-india-girls-secondary-education-completion-lags-boys.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This statistic, presented by BW Education citing UNESCO, points to an ongoing challenge in ensuring equitable access and retention for girls in higher secondary schooling within India's rural landscape.</p><p>What to watch: Policy initiatives aimed at improving girls' secondary education completion rates in rural India.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise, accurate, and reflects the provided source material perfectly.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxQeVA5VmhHdkJ3VjZPek9XRGJnZExMQ3FJekgxbWtPMWdSdTRhX0owYXBGcWFuZ0lYMGhKOFBUT0dBdHBPQzYtQVVHXzhUcU1oazFtODZWQW4yMDVBZy1IYnFVMnBMbHI4UEItQkNYbnpTbXRWNW5hVTVFdmZqSWFUWXlNYnhxM281b0s2MDFvb2xxOEV5TE9kUi14N3VSY0xPa2loV3Z2QnpSZkdPRlJ5LXdfQnJGYXNXbjlOTDF6S1hmblFZ?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
